From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: attrr <110731994+attrr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:58:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_smbx: a hot port's suspend lasts until
 unplugged

Stock's overheat_mitigation keeps USB input off after the port cools
down, until it's unplugged. Disabling Type-C removes VBUS from a
compliant partner, but a legacy cable's stays on: resuming then heats
whatever made the port hot again. Keep the cooling device's USB_IN
suspend while VBUS is present, read from the plugin interrupt's level,
which holds while suspended; an unplug's status change runs the poll
that resumes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 819266ff7168..b2391ba655a0 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -845,6 +845,17 @@ static void smb_watchdog_recover(struct smb_chip *chip)
 	smb_update_charging_enable(chip);
 }
 
+/* VBUS on USB_IN, suspended or not: the plugin interrupt's level */
+static bool smb_usb_present(struct smb_chip *chip)
+{
+	bool present;
+
+	if (irq_get_irqchip_state(chip->cable_irq, IRQCHIP_STATE_LINE_LEVEL,
+				  &present))
+		return true;
+	return present;
+}
+
 /*
  * Stock's charge table (google,chg-{temp,cv,cc}-limits), as its google_battery
  * runs it, every 30s from the battery this charges: its temperature picks a
@@ -868,16 +879,23 @@ static void smb_table_work(struct work_struct *work)
 	unsigned long state = READ_ONCE(chip->therm_state);
 	int therm_ua = state ? chip->therm_limits[state - 1] : 0;
 	int usb_online = 0;
-	bool inhibit = false, changed;
+	bool inhibit = false, changed, suspend;
 
 	/* the watchdog's: from here, charging needs the next poll in time */
 	regmap_write(chip->regmap, chip->base + BARK_BITE_WDOG_PET,
 		     BARK_BITE_WDOG_PET_BIT);
 
-	/* first: suspended, USBIN isn't online */
+	/*
+	 * first: suspended, USBIN isn't online. As stock's overheat_mitigation,
+	 * once the port cools down it stays suspended until unplugged: VBUS
+	 * that a disabled Type-C port doesn't remove (a legacy cable's) heats
+	 * whatever made it hot again
+	 */
 	mutex_lock(&chip->lock);
-	if (chip->therm_suspend != (state && !therm_ua)) {
-		chip->therm_suspend = state && !therm_ua;
+	suspend = (state && !therm_ua) ||
+		  (chip->therm_suspend && smb_usb_present(chip));
+	if (chip->therm_suspend != suspend) {
+		chip->therm_suspend = suspend;
 		dev_info(chip->dev, "cooling: USB input %s\n",
 			 chip->therm_suspend ? "suspended" : "resumed");
 	}
